; A posting whose amount is not a number.
;
; `5.0.0` gets past the regex — which only asks for digits, dots and a sign —
; and fails in the arithmetic that divides a total by the units. Raised from
; there it surfaced as `Invalid literal for Fraction: '5.0.0'`: no file, no
; line, no posting quoted, two branches away from a refusal that quotes all
; three.
;
; What this fixture produces: a refusal naming the transaction, quoting the
; posting, and saying which part of it is not a number.
;
; Verified by tests/integration/test_beancount_reads_what_a_person_writes.py.
2024-01-01 commodity CAD
